# >>> carbon (generated + derived — safe to keep, rebuildable) >>>
# generated tool dirs (materialized copies — stamped, never hand-edited).
# Ignored by CONTENTS (`dir/*`), never as a directory (`dir/`): git refuses to
# descend into an excluded directory, so `.claude/` would make the bootstrap
# shim below impossible to re-include no matter where the negation sits.
.claude/*
.cursor/*
.opencode/*
# …except the ONE committed file per platform that lets a fresh clone self-elect.
# A carbon repo is platform-agnostic, so these folders are otherwise derived;
# without this the clone auto-loads nothing and an agent works off the rails.
!.claude/CLAUDE.md
!.cursor/rules/
.cursor/rules/*
!.cursor/rules/carbon-bootstrap.mdc
# The legacy ROOT memory file: derived, superseded by .claude/CLAUDE.md.
# Anchored with a leading slash — bare `CLAUDE.md` matches at ANY depth, so it
# silently re-ignored .claude/CLAUDE.md (last match wins) and the shim vanished.
/CLAUDE.md
# Cursor configuration may be merged with machine-local user entries at
# materialization time, but the entire native target remains local and derived.
# transient meld state. The LOCK is not here: commit the lock. It records the
# commit each source resolved to, and `carbon-synapse --frozen` replays it.
**/.carbon/.resolved-set.json
**/.carbon/.resolved-set.json.run.*
**/.carbon/store/
**/.carbon/.lock
# derived skill-memory (catalog, BM25 index, knowledge graph, HTML report)
**/.carbon/catalog.json
**/.carbon/index/
**/.carbon/graph/
**/.carbon/graph.json
**/.carbon/report.html
**/.carbon/graph.html
# canonical layout: derived machinery (store, index, graph) lives here, ignored by
# CONTENTS so the lock can be re-included: commit .carbon/derived/lock.json.
**/.carbon/derived/*
!**/.carbon/derived/lock.json
# generated command shims (resolve their own root, but still machine-derived)
**/.carbon/bin/
# cortex run state (frozen plans + journals — regenerable, per-run). Receipts
# are NOT ignored: they are durable proof and belong in the repo.
**/.carbon/cortex/
# the agenthook JOURNAL — operational state, not proof. A per-run receipt is
# evidence that a procedure ran; this appends on EVERY interposition, so left
# committed it grows without bound and lands in every diff forever. syslog does
# not live in git. Narrow by filename so receipts around it stay committed.
**/.carbon/receipts/carbon-guard.jsonl
# opt-in local telemetry (never committed)
**/.carbon/telemetry.jsonl
# exported libraries (rebuildable via `carbon export`; publish from their own repo)
**/.carbon/export/
# staged + built package trees (`carbon package build|export` → packageDir()).
# Same class as export/: a rebuildable copy of content that already lives here.
**/.carbon/packages/
# the governance judge's approval markers. They bind a verdict to the body hash
# of an UNCOMMITTED change, and once that change is committed there is nothing
# left to judge — so this is transient local state, not the durable proof a
# receipt is. Committing it would also let one machine's approval travel.
**/.carbon/governance/
# INBOUND DEPENDENCY CHECKOUTS, fetched by the meld from a `sources:` coordinate.
# Rebuildable from that coordinate and recorded in the lock, so they are derived —
# but a plain `git clone` leaves a .git inside each one, so without this git stages
# them as ORPHAN GITLINKS (mode 160000) with no .gitmodules to back them. Committed,
# that gives a fresh clone empty directories no `submodule update` can ever populate.
**/.carbon/sources/
**/.carbon/self/submodules/
# signing PRIVATE keys — never commit (the public key + carbon.sig.json ARE committed)
carbon.key
**/carbon.key
# <<< carbon <<<

# inbound dependency checkouts — fetched from `sources:` pins, never committed.
# Kept OUTSIDE the carbon block above: spine regenerates that block on every install.
**/.carbon/sources/
**/.carbon/self/submodules/
